ons, the `1.89ⁿ` pathwidth base   would transfer to cutwidth on subcubic graphs, where no base below 2 is   on record (Bentert et al. 2025). - **The question is about linear width** (owner, 2026-11-04): pathwidth is   FPT (`2^{O(k²)} n`, Bodlaender & Kloks 1996; `2^{O(k³)} n`, Bodlaender   1996; cite the held or missing source), so `pw ≤ k` is already   `2^{o(n)}` whenever `k = o(n^{1/2})` or so, and the only regime the   `2^{o(n)}` question concerns is `k = Θ(n)`, where every FPT dependence is   `2^{Ω(n)}` because the problem is NP-hard. Every transfer theorem, the   positive attempt and the hypothesis map are to be stated for `k = Θ(n)`   (hard instances on record: `pw/n` from 0.19 to 0.82 at `n = 125`), and   item 10 records that the sublinear-width regime is settled by FPT. - The driver commits with `git add -A` after each iteration; keep scratch   under `reports/scratch/subexp_pathwidth/` and large files out of git. - Never end a turn on a background wait; long jobs run in the foreground   with bounded polls.   --- PROGRESS.md (most recent iterations at the bottom) --- # loop0014 progress  Plan: `reports/subexp_pathwidth_plan.md` — pathwidth after ETH: a subexponential exact algorithm for pathwidth conditional on the formally verified subexponential `#k`-SAT theorem (restated as a `Prop`, never asserted), or a formalised linear reduction naming what such an algorithm would refute, and a map of the post-ETH hypothesis landscape for width parameters; items in `iterations.md`; rules in `TASK.md`. Gate: `python3 Ralph_Loops/loop0014/gate.py`.  Current: 4/12 SOLVED  ## Setup — 2026-11-04  - Driver, gate and knobs cloned from loop0013 (`sed s/loop0013/loop0014/`);   `allowed_sorries.txt` empty; `max_iterations` 16, item cap 4 h, fix cap   0.75 h, 3 fix attempts, one retry after a network error. - The OpenAI collection is cloned read-only under `~/dev/untrusted/`   (never built, never run from inside); nothing of it is imported into   `lean/`. - Tree clean at launch; 